course: dictionary
lesson: 5697
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning is right. The word log is a good example. Read the words around it to find the clues.
explain: «Noah forgot to log out at the library.» Log is a verb here. Log out means you leave a computer or website that you had entered. The word out is a clue that you are leaving something.
explain: «Cutting a log or a ribbon into pieces always takes one cut fewer than the number of pieces.» Here log means a thick piece of tree trunk. The clues are cutting and pieces, so a log is something you can cut up.
fact: A log can be a thick piece of a tree trunk or big branch that has been cut down.
fact: To log in or log on means to enter a computer or website with your name and password.
fact: A log can also be a written record of what happens, like a reading log at school.
fact: Logging means cutting down trees for wood.
fact: In maths, when you cut a log into pieces, you always need one cut fewer than the number of pieces.
exercise: «Wombats leave their droppings on rocks and logs to mark their area.» What is a log in this sentence? | A written record of the day | *A thick piece of a fallen tree trunk | A password for a computer | A kind of fire
exercise: «Imagine... in the evening you log on to your old school as well.» What does log on mean? | To cut down a tree | To fall asleep | To write a diary entry | *To enter a computer or website with your name and password
exercise: A log is cut into 5 pieces. How many cuts are needed? | 6 | 3 | *4 | 5
test: In the forest, workers are logging to get wood for the town. What does logging mean? | *Cutting down trees for wood | Sitting on a log to rest | Counting the pieces of wood | Writing down what happens each day
test: Ryan writes in his reading log every night. What is a reading log? | A shelf in the library | *A written record of what you have read | A thick piece of wood for the fire | A password for a computer
exam: «Noah forgot to log out at the library.» What does log out mean here? | To sleep like a log | To write a note in a diary | To cut the wood into pieces | *To leave a computer or website you had entered
